<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; Reading path</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: Russia from Rus' to Revolution</h1><p class="ws-lede">The Russian state from the princes of Kiev to the Soviet Union and its end.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/paths/russia-from-rus-to-revolution">Open the path &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the stops in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the stops from 1 (earliest) to 6 (latest), by when each began: a state&#8217;s founding, a person&#8217;s birth, the date of an event.</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Novgorod Republic</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Kievan Rus'</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Grand Duchy of Moscow</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Tsardom of Russia</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Vladimir the Great</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Mongol invasion of Kievan Rus'</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Key terms</h2><p class="ws-how">The path uses these words. Explain each one in your own words.</p><ul class="ws-terms"><li><b>City-state</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><b>Fur trade</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><b>Republic</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>Stop 1, <b>Kievan Rus'</b>. The path begins here because: &#8220;Rurikid princes ruled the first great East Slavic state from Kiev, a federation of principalities on the river route from the Baltic to Byzantium, until the Mongols sacked Kiev in 1240.&#8221; What does this stop tell you about how the story began?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Stop 6, <b>Tsardom of Russia</b>: &#8220;Founded when Ivan IV was crowned the first Tsar of All Russia in 1547, the Tsardom conquered the Volga khanates and crossed Siberia to the Pacific.&#8221; Find one detail on its page that supports this, and one question it leaves open.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Stop 10, <b>Soviet Union</b>: &#8220;Founded in 1922 as the first communist state, it industrialised under Stalin at enormous human cost, rivalled the United States as a superpower and was dissolved in 1991.&#8221; How does this last stop connect to an earlier one?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The path sums itself up as: &#8220;The Russian state from the princes of Kiev to the Soviet Union and its end.&#8221; Which stop shows this best? Explain your choice.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/paths/russia-from-rus-to-revolution. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: Russia from Rus' to Revolution</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the stops in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Kievan Rus' <span>from 882 CE</span></li><li>Vladimir the Great <span>born c. 958 CE</span></li><li>Novgorod Republic <span>from 1136 CE</span></li><li>Mongol invasion of Kievan Rus' <span>1223–1242</span></li><li>Grand Duchy of Moscow <span>from 1263 CE</span></li><li>Tsardom of Russia <span>from 1547 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Key terms</h2><dl class="ws-key-terms"><dt>City-state</dt><dd>The city-state, a city that governs itself and its countryside, was among the earliest forms of state and one of the most inventive.</dd><dt>Fur trade</dt><dd>The fur trade was the commerce in animal pelts, highly valued for clothing and as luxury goods.</dd><dt>Republic</dt><dd>A republic is a state without a monarch, governed as the public’s affair by officials elected for limited terms under law.</dd></dl></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers use details from the pages of the path.</p></section></div></details>
